{"level":30,"time":1794924894955,"pid":23627,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"c88e1464-9a2b-4068-b37d-c2074b8fda66","event":"trace","trace":{"type":"tool","name":"searchText","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab818c82a655c36","parameters":{"query":"select"},"result":{"result":[{"file":"cli.ts","line":85,"text":"if (!(await stat(root)).isDirectory()) throw new Error('Workspace must be a single project directory; select a root explicitly for multi-root workspaces');"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":49,"text":"  const metrics = { inputTokens: 0, outputTokens: 0, usageAvailable: true, modelCalls: 0, toolCalls: 0, durationMs: 0, outputBytes: 0, cost: null as number | null, memoryReuses: 0, functionTries: 0, memoryPurges: 0, memoryQueryRejects: 0, memoryResultsCompacted: 0, memoryResultsRepeated: 0, autoAttachedEvidence: 0, selectionSkip: null as string | null };"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":385,"text":"            // is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — the model"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":389,"text":"            // flagged as such in the selection input, and the deterministic"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":480,"text":"  const memoryInstructions = library ? ` Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: ${JSON.stringify(library.catalog())}. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection —"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":531,"text":"  // A direct-primitive investigation can leave no executed procedure to select."},{"file":"explore.ts","line":546,"text":"          { role: 'system', content: 'Review the completed research and direct primitive calls. If a useful reusable procedure can reproduce relevant cited evidence, propose one typed TypeScript function expression using only the ten sandbox primitives. Parameterize meaningful variations; do not merely wrap one primitive. Return JSON {\"candidate\":null} if none is appropriate, otherwise {\"candidate\":{\"name\":\"TypeScriptIdentifier\",\"question\":\"canonical question\",\"description\":\"ASCII English purpose, scope, output and limits\",\"source\":\"typed function expression\",\"params\":{}}}. Do not invent evidence. The procedure will be executed and validated before selection.' },"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":615,"text":"  const selectionSkip = !library ? null"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":621,"text":"  metrics.selectionSkip = selectionSkip;"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":625,"text":"    // auto-submitted to selection — the model considers their contribution and"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":627,"text":"    // reconciliation loop below and never enter the selection pool."},{"file":"explore.ts","line":629,"text":"    let selected = new Set<string>();"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":631,"text":"      const selectionStarted = new Date();"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":634,"text":"      const selectionInput = { tour: result, catalog: library.catalog(), executedCandidates: eligible.map(attempt => ({ origin: attempt.synthesized ? 'post-research synthesis' : 'research trial', name: attempt.candidate!.name, question: attempt.candidate!.objective, description: attempt.candidate!.description, paramsSchema: attempt.candidate!.paramsSchema, returns: attempt.candidate!.returns, code: attempt.candidate!.code, output: boundedOutput(attempt.output, { revision: currentRevision ?? 'unknown-revision', sourceTruncated: attempt.truncated }) })) };"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":643,"text":"            { role: 'system', content: 'Select executed procedures that contributed to this research or, for post-research synthesis, reproduce relevant cited evidence from it, worked correctly, are clearly documented (purpose, parameters, return and limits), and do not duplicate an existing procedure. Synthesized procedures were not used during research. Project-specific procedures are welcome; do not predict future utility. This result has structural evidence validation only, not semantic verification. Return JSON {\"selected\":[\"name\"]}; select only from the executed candidates below. You may select none. Compare question, scope, inputs, output and limits with existing entries; prefer reuse over duplicates.' },"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":645,"text":"            { role: 'user', content: JSON.stringify(selectionInput) }"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":653,"text":"        const names = (response.result as { selected?: unknown })?.selected;"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":655,"text":"        if (Array.isArray(names) && !stopped) selected = new Set(names.filter((name): name is string => typeof name === 'string'));"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":656,"text":"        recordCall({ type: 'model', name: 'memory-selection', parameters: selectionInput, result: { response: response.result, toolCalls: response.toolCalls, selected: [...selected], budgetStop: stopped ?? null }, inputTokens: usage?.inputTokens ?? null, outputTokens: usage?.outputTokens ?? null, usageMissing: !usage }, selectionStarted, new Date());"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":659,"text":"        recordCall({ type: 'model', name: 'memory-selection', parameters: selectionInput, inputTokens: null, outputTokens: null, usageMissing: true, error: String(error) }, selectionStarted, new Date());"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":693,"text":"      if (!selected.has(candidateName)) {"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":694,"text":"        unreconciled.push({ name: candidateName, proposed: false, replayed: false, accepted: false, reason: 'Not selected by the model for consolidation' });"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":754,"text":"    // rejected with a reason — including candidates the model never selected"},{"file":"memory.ts","line":71,"text":"  /** True when the model proposed (selected) the candidate for consolidation. */"}],"returned":24,"observed":24,"truncated":false,"bounds":{"maxItems":50,"maxBytes":8000},"bytes":7246,"revision":"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780","provenance":"primitive-derived","uncertainty":["Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence."]},"inputTokens":null,"outputTokens":null,"usageMissing":false,"outcome":"keys=result,returned,observed,truncated","runId":"c88e1464-9a2b-4068-b37d-c2074b8fda66","seq":9,