kspace must be a single project directory; select a root explicitly for multi-root workspaces');\"},{\"file\":\"explore.ts\",\"line\":49,\"text\":\"  const metrics = { inputTokens: 0, outputTokens: 0, usageAvailable: true, modelCalls: 0, toolCalls: 0, durationMs: 0, outputBytes: 0, cost: null as number | null, memoryReuses: 0, functionTries: 0, memoryPurges: 0, memoryQueryRejects: 0, memoryResultsCompacted: 0, memoryResultsRepeated: 0, autoAttachedEvidence: 0, selectionSkip: null as string | null };\"},{\"file\":\"explore.ts\",\"line\":385,\"text\":\"            // is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — the model\"},{\"file\":\"explore.ts\",\"line\":389,\"text\":\"            // flagged as such in the selection input, and the deterministic\"},{\"file\":\"explore.ts\",\"line\":480,\"text\":\"  const memoryInstructions = library ? ` Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: ${JSON.stringify(library.catalog())}. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same