{"level":30,"time":1794924906392,"pid":23627,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"c88e1464-9a2b-4068-b37d-c2074b8fda66","event":"trace","trace":{"type":"tool","name":"readLines","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a52afba2300c5723","parameters":{"endLine":420,"file":"explore.ts","startLine":326},"result":{"result":{"file":"explore.ts","start":326,"lines":[{"line":326,"text":"        else if (codeMode && ((call.name === 'code' && typeof call.arguments.code === 'string') || (call.name === 'function_try' && typeof call.arguments.source === 'string') || (library && call.name === 'memory_run' && typeof call.arguments.id === 'string'))) {"},{"line":327,"text":"          const stored = call.name === 'memory_run' ? library?.get(String(call.arguments.id)) : undefined;"},{"line":328,"text":"          if (call.name === 'memory_run' && !stored) throw new Error('Unknown script');"},{"line":329,"text":"          const code = stored?.code ?? String(call.arguments.source ?? call.arguments.code);"},{"line":330,"text":"          const params = call.arguments.params ?? {};"},{"line":331,"text":"          if (!params || typeof params !== 'object' || Array.isArray(params)) throw new Error('Invalid parameters');"},{"line":332,"text":"          const remaining = limits.durationMs - (Date.now() - startedMs);"},{"line":333,"text":"          if (remaining <= 0) return { messages: outputs, stopReason: 'duration' };"},{"line":334,"text":"          const { runScript } = await import('codetour-exploration-sandbox');"},{"line":335,"text":"          const controller = new AbortController();"},{"line":336,"text":"          const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), remaining);"},{"line":337,"text":"          scriptCall = { type: stored ? 'memory_run' : 'function_try', name: stored ? stored.id : 'function_try' };"},{"line":338,"text":"          if (call.name === 'function_try') metrics.functionTries++;"},{"line":339,"text":"          // Ticket #191: any memory_run/function_try call — accepted or failed —"},{"line":340,"text":"          // counts as having served its declared question; the trace carries the"},{"line":341,"text":"          // outcome, the reminder only targets questions never attempted."},{"line":342,"text":"          const runStarted = new Date();"},{"line":343,"text":"          try {"},{"line":344,"text":"            let raw: unknown;"},{"line":345,"text":"            if (stored) {"},{"line":346,"text":"              metrics.memoryReuses++;"},{"line":347,"text":"              // Issue #174 complement (B-verification): stored revision + proof validity"},{"line":348,"text":"              // checked against the fixture — uncertain/obsolete proofs are signalled"},{"line":349,"text":"              // explicitly, never returned silently as fresh."},{"line":350,"text":"              const revision = await resolveRevision();"},{"line":351,"text":"              if (stored.revision && revision !== 'unknown-revision' && !revision.startsWith(stored.revision.slice(0, 12))) {"},{"line":352,"text":"                output = { staleness: { signal: 'stored-revision-differs', storedRevision: stored.revision, currentRevision: revision, note: `Proofs were consolidated at revision ${stored.revision}. Re-verify before relying on them; prefer re-exploring with the permanent primitives if the references below look obsolete.` } };"},{"line":353,"text":"              }"},{"line":354,"text":"            }"},{"line":355,"text":"            const strict = call.name === 'function_try' || stored?.executionMode === 'strict';"},{"line":356,"text":"            const execution = await runScript({ workspace: root, code, params, scripts: strict ? undefined : library?.sources(), strict, includeTrace: true, timeoutMs: Math.min(scriptTimeoutMs, remaining), signal: controller.signal });"},{"line":357,"text":"            raw = execution.value;"},{"line":358,"text":"            sourceIncomplete = execution.trace.truncated;"},{"line":359,"text":"            const runEnded = new Date();"},{"line":360,"text":"            // Compact, structured, bounded, sourced output for memory_run AND function_try."},{"line":361,"text":"            const bounded = boundedOutput(raw, { revision: await resolveRevision(), maxItems: stored?.limits?.maxItems ?? config.memoryOutput.maxItems, maxBytes: stored?.limits?.maxBytes ?? config.memoryOutput.maxBytes, sourceTruncated: execution.trace.truncated, primitiveDerived: execution.trace.executedCalls.length > 0 });"},{"line":362,"text":"            // Issue #185 (D02): every mandatory reference a strict trial emits is"},{"line":363,"text":"            // exhaustively validated without any LLM — no sample, no judge. A"},{"line":364,"text":"            // citation-invalid trial returns short structured repair feedback"},{"line":365,"text":"            // instead of its result, is never proposed for consolidation, and"},{"line":366,"text":"            // leaves its code and diagnostics in the trace only."},{"line":367,"text":"            const citations = call.name === 'function_try' ? await validateCitations(raw, { maxReferences: config.citations.maxReferences, access: citationAccess(tools), revision: await resolveRevision() }) : undefined;"},{"line":368,"text":"            const citationFailure = citations?.status === 'validation_failed' ? citationRepairFeedback(citations) : undefined;"}],"nextLine":369,"truncatedLines":[]},"returned":1,"observed":null,"truncated":false,"bounds":{"maxItems":50,"maxBytes":8000},"bytes":5088,"revision":"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780","provenance":"primitive-derived","uncertainty":["Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence."]},"inputTokens":null,"outputTokens":null,"usageMissing":false,"outcome":"keys=result,returned,observed,truncated","runId":"c88e1464-9a2b-4068-b37d-c2074b8fda66","seq":21,"startedAt":"2026-11-17T14:15:06.139Z","endedAt":"2026-11-17T14:15:06.392Z","durationMs":253}}
{"level":30,"time":1794924906393,"pid":23627,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"c88e1464-9a2b-4068-b37d-c2074b8fda66","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"La question porte sur le mécanisme de mémoire procédurale : comment elle est sélectionnée puis exécutée au cours d'une recherche (retrieval/search).\",\"Il faut identifier le module ou la classe représentant la mémoire procédurale (souvent 'procedural', 'ProceduralMemory', 'production', 'rule' selon les architectures type ACT-R / SOAR / cognitives).\",\"Il faut distinguer deux phases : (1) la sélection (matching/conflict resolution, scoring, seuils, bruit) et (2) l'exécution (firing, application des productions, mise à jour des buffers).\",\"La réponse doit citer des lignes de code précises (fichier + numéros de lignes) pour chaque étape.\",\"Livrable secondaire : une fonction paramétrable et réutilisable qui retrouve tous les appels à un symbole donné (nom de fonction/méthode), avec options (définition vs appels, portée, regex exacte, exclusions).\",\"Le catalogue est vide : aucune fonction réutilisable existante n'est disponible, la fonction de recherche d'appels devra donc être écrite et testée dans cette session.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Localiser les fichiers liés à la mémoire procédurale : grep -rn 'procedural' --include='*.py' (ou extension du langage du projet) pour trouver le module principal.\",\"Chercher les points d'entrée de la boucle de recherche : grep -rn 'def retrieve\\\\|def search\\\\|def select\\\\|def fire\\\\|def execute\\\\|def step' dans le module procédural identifié.\",\"Lire le code de sélection : identifier où les productions candidates sont filtrées/matchées contre l'état courant (buffers, conditions), où le score/utilité est calculé, et où une production gagnante est choisie (noter fichier + lignes exactes).\",\"Lire le code d'exécution : identifier où la production sélectionnée est appliquée (actions, modifications de buffers, effets de bord), et comment le résultat est réinjecté dans la recherche (noter fichier + lignes exactes).\",\"Tracer l'appelant : grep -rn sur le nom des fonctions de sélection/exécution trouvées pour comprendre à quel moment du cycle de recherche elles sont invoquées (ordre d'appel, boucle principale).\",\"Vérifier s'il existe des paramètres de sélection (seuil, température, bruit, utilité) et où ils sont lus, pour enrichir la citation de lignes.\",\"Écrire la fonction réutilisable find_symbol_calls(symbol, root, include_defs=False, pattern='call'|'any', exclude_dirs=[...]) utilisant l'AST du langage si disponible (ast.parse en Python) sinon regex avec détection d'appels, et retourner une liste (fichier, ligne, colonne, extrait).\",\"Tester la fonction sur un symbole connu du module procédural (ex. la fonction de sélection trouvée) et vérifier que les résultats coïncident avec les occurrences trouvées manuellement au grep.\"],\"reuse\":[]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Comment la mémoire procédurale est-elle sélectionnée et exécutée pendant une recherche ? Cite les lignes de code. Propose et essaie aussi une fonction paramétrable réutilisable pour retrouver les appels à un symbole."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0bca4d09bb02618","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb4129bbc6a2991b","type":"function","function":{"name":"memory_list","arguments":"{\"query\":\"procedural memory selection execution search\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0bca4d09bb02618","content":"{\"result\":[\"citation-validator.ts\",\"cli.ts\",\"config.ts\",\"decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"exploration-evidence