or its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Crée et essaie immédiatement une fonction paramétrable réutilisable avec function_try pour rechercher un nom de symbole dans les fichiers TypeScript et renvoyer les références avec lignes. Exemple de paramètre : memory_run. Limite la recherche puis conclus avec les références."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a118fdfbf02f2dc9","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{\"maxFiles\":50}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf6bd090d447b597","type":"function","function":{"name":"memory_list","arguments":"{\"query\":\"search symbol references in TypeScript files\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a118fdfbf02f2dc9","content":"{\"result\":[\".tours/config.json\",\"citation-validator.ts\",\"cli.ts\",\"config.ts\",\"decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"exploration-evidence.ts\",\"exploration-helpers.ts\",\"explore.ts\",\"mask.ts\",\"memory-output.ts\",\"memory.ts\",\"mistral.ts\",\"primitives.ts\",\"research-log.ts\",\"sandbox.d.ts\",\"scratch.ts\",\"summary.ts\",\"tool-contract.ts\",\"workspace.ts\"],\"returned\":19,\"observed\":19,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":320,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf6bd090d447b597","content":"[]"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-848e5b243a374681","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Searches a symbol name across TypeScript files of the workspace and returns each occurrence with file, line number and source text. Scope: all .ts and .tsx files returned by listFiles, excluding .d.ts files and paths containing node_modules, dist, or build. Reads each file page by page with readLines until exhausted. Matches use word-boundary regex so memory_runs does not match memory_run. Result shape: { symbolName, filesScanned, totalMatches, references: [{file, line, text}] }. Limits: syntactic text matches only, no semantic resolution; unreadable files are skipped silently; capped at 200 references per file to bound output.\",\"name\":\"findSymbolReferences\",\"params\":{\"symbolName\":\"memory_run\"},\"question\":\"How to find all textual references of a given symbol name across TypeScript files with file, line number and source text?\",\"returns\":\"{ symbolName: string, filesScanned: number, totalMatches: number, references: { file: string, line: number, text: string }[] }\",\"source\":\"async (params: { symbolName: string; extensions?: string[]; excludePatterns?: string[] }) => {\\n  const symbolName: string = params.symbolName;\\n  const extensions: string[] = params.extensions ?? [\\\".ts\\\", \\\".tsx\\\"];\\n  const excludePatterns: string[] = params.excludePatterns ?? [\\\"node_modules\\\", \\\"dist\\\", \\\"build\\\", \\\".d.ts\\\"];\\n  const listing = listFiles(200);\\n  const files = listing.filter((p: string) =>\\n    extensions.some((ext: string) => p.endsWith(ext)) &&\\n    !excludePatterns.some((pat: string) => p.includes(pat))\\n  );\\n  const references: { file: string; line: number; text: string }[] = [];\\n  const re = new RegExp(\\\"\\\\\\\\b\\\" + symbolName.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\\\]\\\\\\\\]/g, \\\"\\\\\\\\$&\\\") + \\\"\\\\\\\\b\\\");\\n  let filesScanned = 0;\\n  for (const file of files) {\\n    let startLine = 1;\\n    let perFile = 0;\\n    try {\\n      while (perFile < 200) {\\n        const page = readLines(file, startLine, startLine + 99);\\n        for (const l of page.lines) {\\n          if (re.test(l.text)) {\\n            references.push({ file: file, line: l.line, text: l.text.trim().slice(0, 200) });\\n            perFile++;\\n          }\\n        }\\n        if (page.nextLine === null || page.nextLine <= startLine) break;\\n        startLine = page.nextLine;\\n      }\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      // unreadable file: skip\\n    }\\n    filesScanned++;\\n  }\\n  return { symbolName: symbolName, filesScanned: filesScanned, totalMatches: references.length, references: references };\\n}\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-848e5b243a374681","content":"{\"error\":\"TS2339:20:Property 'text' does not exist on type 'string'.\"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-856c1691fb713704","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Searches a symbol name across TypeScript files of the workspace and returns each occurrence with file, line number and source text. Scope: all .ts and .tsx files returned by listFiles, excluding .d.ts files and paths containing node_modules, dist, or build. Reads each file page by page with readLines until exhausted; page.lines are plain strings, line numbers computed from page start. Matches use word-boundary regex so memory_runs does not match memory_run. Result shape: { symbolName, filesScanned, totalMatches, references: [{file, line, text}] }. Limits: syntactic text matches only, no semantic resolution; unreadable files are skipped silently; capped at 200 references per file to bound output.\",\"name\":\"findSymbolReferences\",\"params\":{\"symbolName\":\"memory_run\"},\"question\":\"How to find all textual references of a given symbol name across TypeScript files with file, line number and source text?\",\"returns\":\"{ symbolName: string, filesScanned: number, totalMatches: number, references: { file: string, line: number, text: string }[] }\",\"source\":\"async (params: { symbolName: string; extensions?: string[]; excludePatterns?: string[] }) => {\\n  const symbolName: string = params.s