ith typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection —"},{"file":"explore.ts","line":771,"text":"  if (library && metrics.functionTries + metrics.memoryReuses === 0) progress('memory_unused', { note: 'memory enabled but no function_try or memory_run was attempted: nothing can be consolidated' });"},{"file":"memory-output.ts","line":3,"text":" * calls (memory_run / function_try)."},{"file":"memory.ts","line":257,"text":"    memory_run: (id: string, params: Record<string, unknown> = {}) => {"},{"file":"mistral.ts","line":27,"text":"      { type: 'function', function: { name: 'memory_run', description: 'Run a stored script with new parameters against the current workspace.', parameters: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, params: { type: 'object' } }, required: ['id', 'params'] } } },"},{"file":"mistral.ts","line":89,"text":"          ? { id: call.id, name: 'memory_run', arguments: { id: named.id, params: Object.fromEntries(named.parameters.filter(parameter => args[parameter] !== undefined).map(pa