{"level":30,"time":1794924987880,"pid":25828,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"ddc391ff-2111-4ad2-84b8-7f842341403a","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"L'objectif est de créer une fonction réutilisable et paramétrable via function_try qui recherche un nom de symbole (ex. memory_run) dans les fichiers TypeScript d'un projet.\",\"La fonction doit renvoyer les références trouvées avec les numéros de lignes, puis être testée immédiatement après sa création.\",\"La recherche doit être limitée (fichiers .ts/.tsx, exclusion probable de node_modules et des fichiers de build) pour rester rapide et pertinente.\",\"Le catalogue fourni est vide : aucune fonction existante ne peut être réutilisée directement, tout doit être construit avec function_try.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Définir la signature de la fonction : paramètre symbolName (string, défaut ou exemple memory_run), paramètre optionnel rootDir et extensions cibles ('.ts', '.tsx').\",\"Implémenter la fonction avec function_try : parcourir récursivement les fichiers TypeScript en excluant node_modules, dist, build et *.d.ts si non pertinent.\",\"Pour chaque fichier, lire le contenu ligne par ligne et collecter les correspondances du symbole avec une regex aux limites de mot (\\\\b) pour éviter les faux positifs (ex. memory_runs ne doit pas matcher memory_run).\",\"Structurer le résultat : { file, line, text } pour chaque référence, avec un comptage total et la liste des fichiers analysés.\",\"Exécuter immédiatement la fonction avec le paramètre memory_run pour la tester sur le projet réel.\",\"Vérifier la qualité des résultats : lignes correctes, absence de doublons, gestion des fichiers illisibles (try/catch interne).\",\"Conclure en présentant les références trouvées pour memory_run (fichier, ligne, extrait de code) et valider que la fonction est bien réutilisable avec n'importe quel autre nom de symbole.\"],\"reuse\":[]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Crée et essaie immédiatement une fonction paramétrable réutilisable avec function_try pour rechercher un nom de symbole dans les fichiers TypeScript et renvoyer les références avec lignes. Exemple de paramètre : memory_run. Limite la recherche puis conclus avec les références."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a118fdfbf02f2dc9","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{\"maxFiles\":50}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf6bd090d447b597","type":"function","function":{"name":"memory_list","arguments":"{\"query\":\"search symbol references in TypeScript files\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a118fdfbf02f2dc9","content":"{\"result\":[\".tours/config.json\",\"citation-validator.ts\",\"cli.ts\",\"config.ts\",\"decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"exploration-evidence.ts\",\"exploration-helpers.ts\",\"explore.ts\",\"mask.ts\",\"memory-output.ts\",\"memory.ts\",\"mistral.ts\",\"primitives.ts\",\"research-log.ts\",\"sandbox.d.ts\",\"scratch.ts\",\"summary.ts\",\"tool-contract.ts\",\"workspace.ts\"],\"returned\":19,\"observed\":19,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":320,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf6bd090d447b597","content":"[]"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-848e5b243a374681","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Searches a symbol name across TypeScript files of the workspace and returns each occurrence with file, 