{"level":30,"time":1794925184614,"pid":33141,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"a982d6b4-91be-4adb-b525-3750d2775dc5","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"La question porte sur explore.ts : identifier précisément où les appels à memory_run sont exécutés (fichier, lignes, contexte d'appel).\",\"Le terme memory_run peut apparaître comme définition, import ou site d'appel ; il faut distinguer ces cas et cibler les sites d'exécution réels.\",\"Contraintes explicites : utiliser tôt une fonction de recherche ciblée avec le paramètre memory_run, limiter la sortie à trois références, citer les lignes originales, et conclure dès que la preuve est disponible.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Lancer une recherche ciblée (grep/ripgrep) sur le motif memory_run restreinte au fichier explore.ts, avec un plafond de trois résultats.\",\"Pour chaque référence retournée, lire le contexte autour de la ligne (quelques lignes avant/après) afin de déterminer s'il s'agit d'une définition, d'un import ou d'un appel effectif.\",\"Citer textuellement les lignes originales identifiées comme sites d'exécution des appels memory_run.\",\"Si les trois références suffisent à établir où les appels sont exécutés, conclure immédiatement sans élargir la recherche.\"],\"reuse\":[\"search_code(pattern: string, path?: string, max_results?: number) — recherche ciblée de texte/motif dans les sources, idéale avec pattern=\\\"memory_run\\\" et path=\\\"explore.ts\\\", max_results=3.\",\"read_file_lines(path: string, start: number, end: number) — lecture de plages de lignes pour citer le contexte original autour de chaque référence trouvée.\",\"list_references(symbol: string, path?: string) — si disponible, résout les occurrences d'un symbole (définition vs appels) pour confirmer les sites d'exécution.\"]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: d