{"level":30,"time":1794925301925,"pid":37108,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"b5c13b0b-a2b5-4216-a2dd-30d6e202244d","event":"trace","trace":{"type":"tool","name":"readLines","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-83b1bbd94a8d8d9b","parameters":{"endLine":440,"file":"explore.ts","startLine":320},"result":{"result":{"file":"explore.ts","start":320,"lines":[{"line":320,"text":"          const id = call.arguments.id;"},{"line":321,"text":"          // Issue #187: a proposed candidate may also be abandoned by name —"},{"line":322,"text":"          // a candidate marked unusable never reaches the catalogue."},{"line":323,"text":"          if (!attempts.some(a => a.id === id || a.candidate?.name === id)) throw new Error('Script must have been executed in this run');"},{"line":324,"text":"          unusableIds.add(id);"},{"line":325,"text":"          for (const previous of attempts) if (previous.candidate?.name === id) abandonedAttempts.add(previous);"},{"line":326,"text":"          output = { recordedAfterValidation: true };"},{"line":327,"text":"        }"},{"line":328,"text":"        else if (codeMode && ((call.name === 'code' && typeof call.arguments.code === 'string') || (call.name === 'function_try' && typeof call.arguments.source === 'string') || (library && call.name === 'memory_run' && typeof call.arguments.id === 'string'))) {"},{"line":329,"text":"          const stored = call.name === 'memory_run' ? library?.get(String(call.arguments.id)) : undefined;"},{"line":330,"text":"          if (call.name === 'memory_run' && !stored) throw new Error('Unknown script');"},{"line":331,"text":"          const code = stored?.code ?? String(call.arguments.source ?? call.arguments.code);"},{"line":332,"text":"          const params = call.arguments.params ?? {};"},{"line":333,"text":"          if (!params || typeof params !== 'object' || Array.isArray(params)) throw new Error('Invalid parameters');"},{"line":334,"text":"          const remaining = limits.durationMs - (Date.now() - startedMs);"},{"line":335,"text":"          if (remaining <= 0) return { messages: outputs, stopReason: 'duration' };"},{"line":336,"text":"          const { runScript } = await import('codetour-exploration-sandbox');"},{"line":337,"text":"          const controller = new AbortController();"},{"line":338,"text":"          const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), remaining);"},{"line":339,"text":"          scriptCall = { type: stored ? 'memory_run' : 'function_try', name: stored ? stored.id : 'function_try' };"},{"line":340,"text":"          if (call.name === 'function_try') metrics.functionTries++;"},{"line":341,"text":"          // Ticket #191: any memory_run/function_try call — accepted or failed —"},{"line":342,"text":"          // counts as having served its declared question; the trace carries the"},{"line":343,"text":"          // outcome, the reminder only targets questions never attempted."}],"nextLine":344,"truncatedLines":[]},"returned":1,"observed":null,"truncated":false,"bounds":{"maxItems":50,"maxBytes":8000},"bytes":2654,"revision":"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780","provenance":"primitive-derived","uncertainty":["Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence."]},"inputTokens":null,"outputTokens":null,"usageMissing":false,"outcome":"keys=result,returned,observed,truncated","runId":"b5c13b0b-a2b5-4216-a2dd-30d6e202244d","seq":20,"startedAt":"2026-11-17T14:21:41.699Z","endedAt":"2026-11-17T14:21:41.925Z","durationMs":226}}
{"level":30,"time":1794925301926,"pid":37108,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"b5c13b0b-a2b5-4216-a2dd-30d6e202244d","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"La question porte sur explore.ts : le mécanisme interne de memory_run, c'est-à-dire comment il vérifie la présence d'un résultat en cache, l'exécute ou non, puis stocke/retourne la valeur.\",\"Livrable : une procédure réutilisable créée tôt via function_try, qui recherche un symbole (memory_run, puis les helpers qu'il appelle) et retourne au maximum trois résultats avec les lignes citées.\",\"Contrainte de non-redondance : une plage de lignes déjà lue ne doit pas être relue lors des étapes suivantes.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Étape 1 — Créer tôt la procédure réutilisable avec function_try : chercher le symbole 'memory_run' dans explore.ts, limiter les résultats à 3, exiger les lignes citées (numéro + extrait) pour chaque résultat.\",\"Étape 2 — Lire uniquement la plage de la définition de memory_run indiquée par le meilleur résultat ; noter les numéros de lignes consultés afin de ne pas les relire.\",\"Étape 3 — Identifier dans ce corps les symboles appelés (cache, clé de mémoïsation, fonction cible) ; si un symbole clé n'est pas encore couvert par les lignes déjà lues, relancer function_try sur ce symbole (max 3 résultats, lignes citées).\",\"Étape 4 — Lire les plages restantes nécessaires (définition du cache, logique d'exécution/retour), en excluant tout intervalle déjà consulté à l'étape 2.\",\"Étape 5 — Conclure : décrire le flux d'exécution de memory_run (calcul de clé → consultation du cache → exécution de la fonction mémorisée si absente → stockage → retour), chaque affirmation appuyée par une citation de ligne.\"],\"reuse\":[]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans explore.ts, explique comment memory_run exécute une fonction mémorisée. Crée tôt avec function_try une procédure réutilisable cherchant un symbole, avec trois résultats au plus et lignes citées. Après lecture des preuves, conclus ; ne relis pas des plages déjà consultées."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a75e9d5e206925fa","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a given symbol identifier and returns at most 3 results with cited line numbers and text excerpts. Uses searchIdentifiers and searchText, deduplicates by file+line, and returns {file, line, text} entries. Limit: 3 results; syntactic matches only, no semantic resolution.\",\"name\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"params\":{\"limit\":3,\"symbol\":\"memory_run\"},\"question\":\"How does memory_run in explore.ts execute a memorized function (cache lookup, execution, storage, return)?\",\"returns\":\"Array of at most 3 objects {file: string, line: number, text: string} citing occurrences of the symbol\",\"source\":\"(symbol: string, limit: number = 3) => {\\n  const byId = searchIdentifiers(symbol).map(r => ({file: r.file, line: r.line, text: (r.text || '').slice(0, 160)}));\\n  const byText = searchText(symbol).map(r => ({file: r.file, line: r.line, text: (r.text || '').slice(0, 160)}));\\n  const seen = new Set<string>();\\n  const out: {file: string, line: number, text: string}[] = [];\\n  for (const r of [...byId, ...byText]) {\\n    const key = r.file + ':' + r.line;\\n    if (seen.has(key)) continue;\\n    seen.add(key);\\n    out.push(r);\\n    if (out.length >= limit) break;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a75e9d5e206925fa","content":"{\"error\":\"TS2345:1:Trial params do not match the function parameter type. Expected string; received { limit: number; symbol: string; }.\"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a0bef476c1d9f99","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a given symbol identifier and returns at most 3 results with cited line numbers and text excerpts. Uses searchIdentifiers and searchText, deduplicates by file+line, and returns {file, line, text} entries. Limit: 3 results; syntactic matches only, no semantic resolution.\",\"name\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"params\":{\"limit\":3,\"symbol\":\"memory_run\"},\"question\":\"How does memory_run in explore.ts execute a memorized function (cache lookup, execution, storage, return)?\",\"returns\":\"Array of at most 3 objects {file: string, line: number, text: string} citing occurrences of the symbol\",\"source\":\"(params: {symbol: string, limit?: number}) => {\\n  const limit = params.limit ?? 3;\\n  const byId = searchIdentifiers(params.symbol).map(r => ({file: r.file, line: r.line, text: (r.text || '').slice(0, 160)}));\\n  const byText = searchText(params.symbol).map(r => ({file: r.file, line: r.line, text: (r.text || '').slice(0, 160)}));\\n  const seen = new Set<string>();\\n  const out: {file: string, line: number, text: string}[] = [];\\n  for (const r of [...byId, ...byText]) {\\n    const key = r.file + ':' + r.line;\\n    if (seen.has(key)) continue;\\n    seen.add(key);\\n    out.push(r);\\n    if (out.length >= limit) break;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a0bef476c1d9f99","content":"{\"error\":\"invalid_citation: 1 of 3 references invalid\",\"validation\":{\"status\":\"validation_failed\",\"message\":\"The trial is NOT validated: 2 of 3 references are valid (first 2 listed). Fix only the faulty reference(s) below, then call function_try again with corrected code.\",\"validCount\":2,\"validReferences\":[{\"file\":\"exploration-helpers.ts\",\"startLine\":28,\"endLine\":28},{\"file\":\"exploratio