{"level":30,"time":1794925788863,"pid":50650,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"35fadf41-ba5e-4657-a5fb-995321c87e6c","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"Identifierer funktionen parseConfig i config.ts som målet for undersøgelsen.\",\"Afgræn spørgsmålet: hvordan håndterer parseConfig ukendte sektioner (top-level nøgler) og ukendte parametre (nøgler inden for kendte sektioner) - dvs. om de afvises, ignoreres, logges eller fejler.\",\"Notér at svaret skal understøttes af direkte citater med linjenumre og tydelige grænser for, hvad koden beviser og ikke beviser.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Kald findSymbolOccurrences med symbol='parseConfig' og limit=10 for at lokalisere alle forekomster, herunder definitionen i config.ts.\",\"Ud fra forekomstlinjerne skal du identificere funktionsdefinitionen og aflæse dens omtrentlige omfang (start- og slutlinje) i config.ts.\",\"Læs funktionslegemet linje for linje og find valideringslogikken: whitelist/allowlist af kendte sektioner, loops over nøgler, og eventuelle fejl- eller advarselskald ved ukendte nøgler.\",\"Skeln eksplicit mellem håndtering af (a) ukendte top-level sektioner og (b) ukendte parametre inden for kendte sektioner, da logikken kan være forskellig.\",\"Notér præcise citater (fil, linje, tekst) for hver relevant beslutning: afvisning, ignorering, standardværdi eller exception.\",\"Tjek om parseConfig kaldes fra loadConfig eller andre funktioner, og om konteksten (f.eks. strict-mode flag) påvirker adfærden; inkluder kun det der er nødvendigt for spørgsmålet.\",\"Formuler konklusionen med citater og angiv grænser: hvad der er verificeret i koden versus hvad der kræver runtime-test (f.eks. faktiske fejlmeddelelser).\"],\"reuse\":[{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: [{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans config.ts, comment parseConfig contrôle-t-elle les sections et paramètres de configuration inconnus ? Utilise la fonction en mémoire findSymbolOccurrences avec le symbole parseConfig pour localiser le code, puis vérifie les lignes pertinentes et réponds avec les citations et limites."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5ae6842f5217924","type":"function","function":{"name":"memory_run","arguments":"{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"params\":{\"limit\":10,\"symbol\":\"parseConfig\"}}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb0135c7136352b3","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5ae6842f5217924","content":"{\"result\":[{\"file\":\"config.ts\",\"line\":43,\"text\":\"export function parseConfig(raw: unknown): HarnessConfig {\"},{\"file\":\"config.ts\",\"line\":69,\"text\":\"  try { return parseConfig(JSON.parse(text)); }\"}],\"returned\":2,\"observed\":2,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":188,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb0135c7136352b3","content":"{\"result\":[\".tours/.memory/b6f7ac2cdf7e9cfd6f12eaffefc3ebd7676d1e8405d5890db286e7a71df9299e.json\",\".tours/.memory/functions/findSymbolOccurrences.ts\",\".tours/config.json\",\"citation-validator.ts\",\"cli.ts\",\"config.ts\",\"decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"exploration-evidence.ts\",\"exploration-helpers.ts\",\"explore.ts\",\"mask.ts\",\"memory-output.ts\",\"memory.ts\",\"mistral.ts\",\"primitives.ts\",\"research-log.ts\",\"sandbox.d.ts\",\"scratch.ts\",\"summary.ts\",\"tool-contract.ts\",\"workspace.ts\"],\"returned\":21,\"observed\":21,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":459,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b78611a8168d4a44","type":"function","function":{"name":"readLines","arguments":"{\"endLine\":110,\"file\":\"config.ts\",\"startLine\":1}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b78611a8168d4a44","content":"{\"omitted\":true,\"note\":\"Already read, result omitted to save context: readLines({\\\"endLine\\\":110,\\\"file\\\":\\\"config.ts\\\",\\\"startLine\\\":1}). Full result saved as chatcmpl-tool-b78611a8168d4a44; use readScratch with resultId and offset 0 if needed. Cite original sources. Rely on what you noted.\",\"bytes\":2984,\"head\":\"{\\\"result\\\":{\\\"file\\\":\\\"config.ts\\\",\\\"start\\\":1,\\\"lines\\\":[{\\\"line\\\":1,\\\"text\\\":\\\"import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\\\"},{\\\"line\\\":2,\\\"text\\\":\\\"import { join } from 'node:path';\\\"},{\\\"line\\\":3,\\\"text\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"line\\\":4,\\\"text\\\":\\\"export type ReasoningEffort = 'low' | 'medium' | 'high' | 'max';\\\"},{\\\"line\\\":5,\\\"text\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"lin\"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5e1024e5690c967","type":"function","function":{"name":"readLines","arguments":"{\"endLine\":90,\"file\":\"config.ts\",\"startLine\":33}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5e1024e5690c967","content":"{\"omitted\":true,\"note\":\"Already read, result omitted to save context: readLines({\\\"endLine\\\":90,\\\"file\\\":\\\"config.ts\\\",\\\"startLine\\\":33}). Full result saved as chatcmpl-tool-a5e1024e5690c967; use readScratch with resultId and offset 0 if needed. Cite original sources. Rely on what you noted.\",\"bytes\":2995,\"head\":\"{\\\"result\\\":{\\\"file\\\":\\\"config.ts\\\",\\\"start\\\":33,\\\"lines\\\":[{\\\"line\\\":33,\\\"text\\\":\\\"  if (!overrides || typeof overrides !== 'object' || Array.isArray(overrides)) throw new Error(`${path} must be an object`);\\\"},{\\\"line\\\":34,\\\"text\\\":\\\"  const result: Record<string, any> = { ...defaults };\\\"},{\\\"line\\\":35,\\\"text\\\":\\\"  for (co\"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c7ef0ec904ed861","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Extracts structured evidence about unknown-key handling in a config parser. Runs searchText for given patterns, dedupes by file:line, and returns matching lines with their text. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: maxPatterns capped at 5, results capped at 20 items.\",\"name\":\"extractUnknownKeyHandling\",\"params\":{\"file\":\"config.ts\",\"patterns\":[\"Unknown section\",\"Unknown setting\",\"in DEFAULT_CONFIG\",\"in defaults\"]},\"question\":\"How does parseConfig in config.ts reject unknown sections and unknown settings?\",\"source\":\"async ({ file, patterns }: { file: string; patterns: string[] }) => {\\n  const seen = new Set<string>();\\n  const out: { file: string; line: number; text: string; pattern: string }[] = [];\\n  for (const pattern of patterns.slice(0, 5)) {\\n    const hits = await searchText(pattern);\\n    for (const h of hits) {\\n      if (h.file !== file) continue;\\n      const id = `${h.file}:${h.line}`;\\n      if (seen.has(id)) continue;\\n      seen.add(id);\\n      out.push({ file: h.file, line: h.line, text: h.text, pattern });\\n      if (out.length >= 20) return out;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c7ef0ec904ed861","content":"{\"result\":{},\"returned\":1,\"observed\":null,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":2,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-96da5172a3ce2e46","type":"function","function":{"name":"searchText","arguments":"{\"query\":\"Unknown section\"}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80a3263fc712c7ff","type":"function"