{"level":30,"time":1794926024032,"pid":57472,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"42314447-9d56-48a8-9f65-524447ee5783","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"Identifier dans cli.ts comment les arguments de la ligne de commande sont parsés (parsing, options, sous-commandes).\",\"Déterminer comment ces arguments sont transformés en paramètres d'entrée pour explore (mapping, validation, valeurs par défaut).\",\"Repérer le point d'appel exact où explore est invoqué depuis cli.ts et le contexte de cet appel.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Utiliser findSymbolOccurrences avec symbol=\\\"explore\\\" et limit=10 pour localiser toutes les occurrences d'explore, notamment dans cli.ts.\",\"Lire cli.ts autour des occurrences trouvées : bloc de parsing des arguments (argv, flags, options) et construction de la configuration passée à explore.\",\"Lire la signature de explore (fichier de définition) pour vérifier la correspondance entre les arguments CLI et les paramètres attendus.\",\"Vérifier s'il existe une étape intermédiaire (normalisation, validation, chargement de config) entre le parsing CLI et l'appel à explore.\"],\"reuse\":[{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: [{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\