 .tours/config.json holds every setting; CLI options override it per run. Only the API key may also come from the environment."},{"line":94,"text":"const config = await loadConfig(root);"},{"line":95,"text":"const effectiveTemperature = temperature ?? config.mistral.temperature;"},{"line":96,"text":"if (!Number.isFinite(effectiveTemperature) || effectiveTemperature < 0 || effectiveTemperature > 1) throw new Error('Temperature must be between 0 and 1');"},{"line":97,"text":"model = mistral(process.env.MISTRAL_API_KEY || config.mistral.apiKey, modelName ?? config.mistral.model, { ...config.mistral, temperature: effectiveTemperature });"}],"nextLine":null,"truncatedLines":[]},"returned":1,"observed":null,"truncated":false,"bounds":{"maxItems":50,"maxBytes":8000},"bytes":2357,"revision":"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780","provenance":"primitive-derived","uncertainty":["Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence."]},"inputTokens":null,"outputTokens":null,"usageMissing":false,"outcome":"keys=result,returned,observed,truncated","runId":"42314447-9d56-48a8-9f65-524447ee5783","seq":22,"startedAt":"2026-11-17T14:33:52.003Z","endedAt":"2026-11-17T14:33:52.237Z","durationMs":234}}
{"level":30,"time":1794926032240,"pid":57472,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"42314447-9d56-48a8-9f65-524447ee5783","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"Identifier dans cli.ts comment les arguments de la ligne de commande sont parsés (parsing, options, sous-commandes).\",\"Déterminer comment ces arguments sont transformés en paramètres d'entrée pour explore (mapping, validation, valeurs par défaut).\",\"Repérer le point d'appel exact où explore est invoqué depuis cli.ts et le contexte de cet appel.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Utiliser findSymbolOccurrences avec symbol=\\\"explore\\\" et limit=10 pour localiser toutes les occurrences d'explore, notamment dans cli.ts.\",\"Lire cli.ts autour des occurrences trouvées : bloc de parsing des arguments (argv, flags, options) et construction de la configuration passée à explore.\",\"Lire la signature de explore (fichier de définition) pour vérifier la correspondance entre les arguments CLI et les paramètres attendus.\",\"Vérifier s'il existe une étape intermédiaire (normalisation, validation, chargement de config) entre le parsing CLI et l'appel à explore.\"],\"reuse\":[{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: [{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans cli.ts, comment les arguments de la CLI préparent-ils et lancent-ils explore ? Utilise findSymbolOccurrences pour localiser explore puis lis les passages nécessaires. Fournis le JSON final avec les citations et les éventuelles limites dès que ce mécanisme est établi."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8912344365ec04e2","type":"function","function":{"name":"memory_run","arguments":"{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"params\":{\"limit\":10,\"symbol\":\"explore\"}}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b226904a99ee8fcd","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8912344365ec04e2","content":"{\"omitted\":true,\"note\":\"Already read, result omitted to save context