{"level":30,"time":1794926150963,"pid":62423,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"4ce6b7ad-a280-491f-8aa8-3bce6342de82","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"La question porte sur une seule fonction : loadConfig dans config.ts.\",\"Deux points à élucider : (1) le mécanisme de chargement du fichier de configuration (lecture disque, parsing, format attendu), (2) le comportement en cas d'absence du fichier (exception, valeur par défaut, message d'erreur, exit).\",\"La réponse doit citer les lignes pertinentes de config.ts et signaler explicitement toute incertitude (ex. : comportement dépendant d'un appelant, code non visible, gestion d'erreur déléguée ailleurs).\"],\"investigate\":[\"Localiser config.ts dans le dépôt et lire la définition de loadConfig en entier, en notant les numéros de lignes exacts.\",\"Identifier l'appel de lecture de fichier utilisé (fs.readFileSync, fs.promises.readFile, import dynamique, etc.) et le chemin/résolution du fichier de configuration.\",\"Repérer la gestion d'erreur : try/catch, vérification d'existence (existsSync), valeur de repli, throw, ou propagation silencieuse ; noter les numéros de lignes correspondants.\",\"Vérifier s'il existe des tests ou des appelants de loadConfig qui confirment le comportement en cas de fichier manquant.\",\"Consigner toute ambiguïté restante (ex. : comportement différent selon l'environnement, code d'une dépendance non inspectée) et la mentionner comme incertitude dans la réponse.\"],\"reuse\":[{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"why\":\"Permet de trouver rapidement toutes les occurrences de loadConfig (définition et appelants) avec fichier et numéro de ligne, ce qui fournit les citations de lignes demandées et aide à confirmer le comportement en cas de fichier manquant via les appelants/tests.\",\"suggestedParameters\":{\"symbol\":\"loadConfig\",\"limit\":10}}]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: [{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stab