s, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection —\"},{\"file\":\"primitives.ts\",\"line\":174,\"text\":\" * searchIdentifiers - Search for exact identifier matches\"},{\"file\":\"primitives.ts\",\"line\":518,\"text\":\"  searchIdentifiers(identifier: string, options?: SearchIdentifiersOptions): Promise<SearchIdentifiersResult>;\"},{\"file\":\"tool-contract.ts\",\"line\":7,\"text\":\"  { name: 'searchIdentifiers', description: 'Find exact identifier occurrences', properties: { identifier: string }, required: ['identifier'] },\"},{\"file\":\"workspace.ts\",\"line\":237,\"text\":\"  // searchIdentifiers - Search for exact identifier matches\"},{\"file\":\"workspace.ts\",\"line\"