ore n'apparaît pas dans 90-112, le consigner comme incertitude : indiquer ce qui est visible dans la plage (ex. fin du préflight, préparation des arguments) et signaler que l'appel effectif se trouve probablement hors périmètre.\",\"Produire immédiatement le JSON final : références au format cli.ts:ligne pour chaque constat, champ incertitudes listant tout ce qui n'est pas vérifiable dans la plage (définition d'explore, comportement en cas d'échec du préflight, imports).\"],\"reuse\":[{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"reason\":\"Utilisable en secours si l'appel à explore n'est pas visible dans les lignes 90-112 : rechercher les occurrences de 'explore' (ou d'un symbole comme runExplore) dans cli.ts pour localiser la ligne exacte à citer, sans élargir la lecture au-delà du nécessaire.\",\"suggestedParameters\":{\"symbol\":\"explore\",\"limit\":5},\"caveat\":\"Recherche syntaxique par identifiant/littéral : ne résout pas la sémantique (import vs définition locale) ; à utiliser seulement pour ancrer une référence ligne, pas pour conclure sur le mécanisme.\"}]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: [{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. Before concluding, run at least one function_try that composes several primitives or filters their results into structured, cited evidence for this question: it is the only way a reusable procedure can reach memory. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans cli.ts, comment la CLI lance-t-elle explore après le préflight ? Examine uniquement les lignes 90 à 112, puis donne immédiatement une réponse JSON avec références et incertitudes."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b953c31b8e36637a","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a99d1d8f01e4ad13","type":"function","function":{"name":"searchIdentifiers","arguments":"{\"identifier\":\"explore\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b953c31b8e36637a","content":"{\"result\":[\".tours/.memory/b6f7ac2cdf7e9cfd6f12eaffefc3ebd7676d1e8405d5890db286e7a71df9299e.json\",\".tours/.memory/functions/findSymbolOccurrences.ts\",\".tours/config.json\",\"citation-validator.ts\",\"cli.ts\",\"config.ts\",\"decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"exploration-evidence.ts\",\"exploration-helpers.ts\",\"explore.ts\",\"mask.ts\",\"memory-output.ts\",\"memory.ts\",\"mistral.ts\",\"primitives.ts\",\"research-log.ts\",\"sandbox.d.ts\",\"scratch.ts\",\"summary.ts\",\"tool-contract.ts\",\"workspace.ts\"],\"returned\":21,\"observed\":21,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":459,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a99d1d8f01e4ad13","content":"{\"omitted\":true,\"note\":\"Already read, result omitted to save context: searchIdentifiers({\\\"identifier\\\":\\\"explore\\\"}). Full result saved as chatcmpl-tool-a99d1d8f01e4ad13; use readScratch with resultId and offset 0 if needed. Cite original sources. Rely on what you noted.\",\"bytes\":2299,\"head\":\"{\\\"result\\\":[{\\\"file\\\":\\\"cli.ts\\\",\\\"line\\\":7,\\\"text\\\":\\\"import { explore } from './explore.ts';\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"cli.ts\\\",\\\"line\\\":12,\\\"text\\\":\\\"import type { Budget, Model } from './explore.ts';\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"cli.ts\\\",\\\"line\\\":111,\\\"text\\\":\\\"const result = await explore({ root, objective, codeMode, memory, budget, model, config, \"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-91e7697aacb3058c","type":"function","function":{"name":"readLines","arguments":"{\"endLine\":112,\"file\":\"cli.ts\",\"startLine\":90}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91e7697aacb3058c","content":"{\"result\":{\"file\":\"cli.ts\",\"start\":90,\"lines\":[{\"line\":90,\"text\":\"const canonicalMemory = join(root, '.tours', '.memory');\"},{\"line\":91,\"text\":\"if (legacyMemory && resolve(legacyMemory) !== canonicalMemory) throw new Error(`Memory must be stored at ${canonicalMemory}`);\"},{\"line\":92,\"text\":\"const memory = memoryEnabled ? { directory: canonicalMemory } : undefined;\"},{\"line\":93,\"text\":\"// .tours/config.json holds every setting; CLI options override it per run. Only the API key may also come from the environment.\"},{\"line\":94,\"text\":\"const config = await loadConfig(root);\"},{\"line\":95,\"text\":\"const effectiveTemperature = temperature ?? config.mistral.temperature;\"},{\"line\":96,\"text\":\"if (!Number.isFinite(effectiveTemperature) || effectiveTemperature < 0 || effectiveTemperature > 1) throw new Error('Temperature must be between 0 and 1');\"},{\"line\":97,\"text\":\"model = mistral(process.env.MISTRAL_API_KEY || config.mistral.apiKey, modelName ?? config.mistral.model, { ...config.mistral, temperature: effectiveTemperature });\"},{\"line\":98,\"text\":\"if (codeMode) {\"},{\"line\":99,\"text\":\"  // Exercise the real sandbox before starting a model run, including QuickJS and TypeScript.\"},{\"line\":100,\"text\":\"  const { runScript } = await import('codetour-exploration-sandbox');\"},{\"line\":101,\"text\":\"  try { await runScript({ workspace: root, code: '() => 1', params: {}, strict: true, timeoutMs: config.limits.scriptTimeoutMs }); }\"},{\"line\":102,\"text\":\"  catch (error) { throw new Error(`Sandbox preflight failed: ${(error as Error).message}`); }\"},{\"line\":103,\"text\":\"}\"},{\"line\":104,\"text\":\"// Progress is appended as JSON lines next to the output file so a long run can be followed with tail -f.\"},{\"line\":105,\"text\":\"let onProgress: ((event: Record<string, unknown>) => void) | undefined;\"},{\"line\":106,\"text\":\"if (outputFile) {\"},{\"line\":107,\"text\":\"  const progressFile = `${outputFile}.progress`;\"},{\"line\":108,\"text\":\"  await writeFile(progressFile, '');\"},{\"line\":109,\"text\":\"  onProgress = event => appendFileSync(progressFile, `${JSON.stringify(event)}\\\\n`);\"},{\"line\":110,\"text\":\"}\"},{\"line\":111,\"text\":\"const result = await explore({ root, objective, codeMode, memory, budget, model, config, onProgress });\"},{\"line\":112,\"text\":\"await emit(result);\"}],\"nextLine\":null,\"truncatedLines\":[]},\"returned\":1,\"observed\":null,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":2291,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2b9c3104cc41aa3","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Reads a bounded line range of a CLI file and returns structured evidence entries for lines matching given regex patterns (e.g. preflight, explore call). Scope: syntactic line filtering only, no semantic resolution. Returns {file, line, text, matchedPattern}[] capped by limit; patterns that match nothing are reported as unmatched.\",\"name\":\"extractPreflightToExploreEvidence\",\"params\":{\"endLine\":112,\"file\":\"cli.ts\",\"patterns\":[\"preflight\",\"runScript\",\"explore\\\\(\"],\"startLine\":90},\"question\":\"How does the CLI in cli.ts launch explore after the preflight (lines 90-112)?\",\"source\":\"return async ({ file, startLine, endLine, patterns, limit = 20 }: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number; patterns: string[]; limit?: number }) => {\\n  const page = await readLines(file, startLine, endLine);\\n  const out: { file: string; line: number; text: string; matchedPattern: string }[] = [];\\n  const matched = new Set<string>();\\n  for (const l of page.lines) {\\n    for (const p of patterns) {\\n      if (new RegExp(p).test(l.text)) {\\n        out.push({ file: page.file, line: l.line, text: l.text, matchedPattern: p });\\n        matched.add(p);\\n        break;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (out.length >= limit) break;\\n  }\\n  const unmatched = patterns.filter(p => !matched.has(p));\\n  return { evidence: out, unmatchedPatterns: unmatched, nextPage: page.nextLine, truncatedLines: page.truncatedLines.length };\\n};\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2b9c3104cc41aa3","content":"{\"error\":\"TS1108:1:A 'return' statement can only be used within a function body.\"}"}],"options":{"maxOutputTokens":16384,"codeMode":true,"memory":true}}
{"level":30,"time":1794926494449,"pid":74253,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"b0806947-f058-4675-b26f-b86dfee8f91b","event":"model_response","response":{"toolCalls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98d5c52cc76f32ab","name":"function_try","arguments":{"description":"Reads a bounded line range of a CLI file and returns structured evidence entries for lines matching given regex patterns (e.g. preflight, explore call). Scope: syntactic line filtering only, no semantic resolution. Returns {file, line, text, matchedPattern}[] capped by limit; patterns that match nothing are reported as unmatched.","name":"extractPreflightToExploreEvidence","params":{"endLine":112,"file":"cli.ts","patterns":["preflight","runScript","explore\\("],"startLine":90},"question":"How does the CLI in cli.ts launch explore after the preflight (lines 90-112)?","source":"async ({ file, startLine, endLine, patterns, limit = 20 }: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number; patterns: string[]; limit?: number }) => {\n  const page = await readLines(file, startLine, endLine);\n  const out: { file: string; line: number; text: string; matchedPattern: string }[] = [];\n  const matched = new Set<string>();\n  for (const l of page.lines) {\n    for (const p of patterns) {\n      if (new RegExp(p).test(l.text)) {\n        out.push({ file: page.file, line: l.line, text: l.text, matchedPattern: p });\n        matched.add(p);\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n    if (out.length >= limit) break;\n  }\n  const unmatched = patterns.filter(p => !matched.has(p));\n  return { evidence: out, unmatchedPatterns: unmatched, nextPage: page.nextLine, truncatedLines: page.truncatedLines.length };\n}"}}],"usage":{"inputTokens":4354,"outputTokens":373}},"model":{"model":"zai-glm-5-3-flash","temperature":0,"maxOutputTokens":16384}}
