{"level":30,"time":1794926652704,"pid":78641,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"b578dd37-5ed6-4fff-b3fd-169fd4ed2544","event":"model_response","response":{"result":{"candidate":{"name":"traceGatedCallSequence","question":"In a given file and line range, how does the code sequence a gate block (e.g., a preflight check) before invoking a target function, and what runs in between?","description":"Reads a specified line range of a file, locates occurrences of a gate symbol (e.g., a preflight helper like runScript) and a target symbol (e.g., explore) within that range, and returns the ordered statements from the range so the caller can see whether the target call is sequential after the gate, guarded, or absent. Also reports whether the gate is conditional (an enclosing if on the gate's opening line) and whether any early return or throw separates gate from target. Scope: syntactic evidence from one file range plus symbol occurrence lines; no cross-file semantic resolution. Limits: range capped at 200 lines, occurrence lists capped by limit (default 5).","source":"async ({ file, startLine, endLine, gateSymbol, targetSymbol, limit }: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number; gateSymbol: string; targetSymbol: string; limit?: number }): Promise<{ file: string; range: { startLine: number; endLine: number }; lines: { line: number; text: string }[]; gateOccurrences: { file: string; line: number; text: string }[]; targetOccurrences: { file: string; line: number; text: string }[]; gateIsConditional: boolean; targetAfterGate: boolean | null; uncertainty: string[] }> => { const cappedEnd = Math.min(endLine, startLine + 199); const read = await readLines({ file, startLine, endLine: cappedEnd }); const lines = read.result.lines; const cap = limit ?? 5; const gateOcc = (await findSymbolOccurrences({ symbol: gateSymbol, limit: cap })).result.filter(o => o.file === file && o.line >= startLine && o.line <= cappedEnd); const targetOcc = (await findSymbolOccurrences({ symbol: targetSymbol, limit: cap })).result.filter(o => o.file === file && o.line >= startLine && o.line <= cappedEnd); const gateLines = gateOcc.map(o => o.line); const targetLines = targetOcc.map(o => o.line); const gateIsConditional = lines.some(l => gateLines.some(g => g >= l.line && g <= l.line + 1) && /\\bif\\s*\\(/.test(l.text)); const lastGate = gateLines.length ? Math.max(...gateLines) : null; const firstTarget = targetLines.length ? Math.min(...targetLines) : null; const targetAfterGate = lastGate !== null && firstTarget !== null ? firstTarget > lastGate : null; const between = lastGate !== null && firstTarget !== null ? lines.filter(l => l.line > lastGate && l.line < firstTarget) : []; const uncertainty = [ 'Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.', 'Definitions of the gate and target symbols outside the range are not resolved.', 'Conditional detection is heuristic: an if on the gate line or the line above.' ]; if (between.some(l => /\\breturn\\b|\\bthrow\\b/.test(l.text))) uncertainty.push('A return or throw appears between gate and target; the sequential link may be conditional.'); return { file, range: { startLine, endLine: cappedEnd }, lines, gateOccurrences: gateOcc, targetOccurrences: targetOcc, gateIsConditional, targetAfterGate, uncertainty }; }","params":{"file":"cli.ts","startLine":90,"endLine":112,"gateSymbol":"runScript","targetSymbol":"explore","limit":5}}},"usage":{"inputTokens":1706,"outputTokens":1053}},"model":{"model":"zai-glm-5-3-flash","temperature":0,"maxOutputTokens":16384}}
