{"level":30,"time":1794926711156,"pid":80293,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"519aaf5c-3720-484c-95f9-6d3833b18d48","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"Cible : explore.ts, branche de code autour des lignes 334-380 traitant de memory_run.\",\"Question technique unique : comment memory_run retrouve une fonction enregistrée (mécanisme de lookup) et comment il l'exécute (appel/invocation).\",\"Livrable : réponse JSON concise avec citations (fichier:ligne) et incertitudes explicites.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Ouvrir explore.ts et lire la plage ~334-380 pour identifier la branche qui gère memory_run (dispatch/switch ou if).\",\"Repérer la structure d'enregistrement des fonctions (registre, map, objet) : comment la clé/nom passé à memory_run est résolue vers la fonction.\",\"Identifier l'appel effectif : signature, passage d'arguments, gestion du cas 'fonction introuvable' (erreur, fallback).\",\"Noter les numéros de lignes exacts pour les citations et vérifier si le lookup dépend d'un état défini ailleurs dans explore.ts (hors plage 334-380) — à signaler comme incertitude si non confirmé.\"],\"reuse\":[{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"justification\":\"Recherche syntaxique de 'memory_run' dans explore.ts pour localiser précisément sa définition et ses occurrences (y compris la branche ~334-380) avant la lecture ciblée.\",\"suggestedParameters\":{\"symbol\":\"memory_run\",\"limit\":10}}]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: [{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}]. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. When a reusable procedure would add value and no stored procedure or primitive already covers it, try function_try to compose primitives into structured, cited evidence. Do not create a function merely to satisfy a quota; conclude when the evidence is sufficient. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans explore.ts, comment memory_run retrouve-t-il une fonction enregistrée et la lance-t-il ? Lis la branche concernée autour des lignes 334-380, puis retourne une réponse JSON concise avec citations ; indique les incertitudes."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8f5fed82d7b5c86","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b54de82f1645334d","type":"function","function":{"name":"searchIdentifiers","arguments":"{\"identifier\":\"memory_run\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8f5fed82d7b5c86","content":"{\"result\":[\".tours/.memory/b6f7ac2cdf7e9cfd6f12eaffefc3ebd7676d1e8405d5890db286e7a71df9299e.json\",\".tours/.memory/functions/findSymbolOccurrences.ts\",\".tours/config.json\",\"citation-validator.ts\",\"cli.ts\",\"config.ts\",\"decomposition-prompt.ts\",\"exploration-evidence.ts\",\"exploration-helpers.ts\",\"explore.ts\",\"mask.ts\",\"memory-output.ts\",\"memory.ts\",\"mistral.ts\",\"primitives.ts\",\"research-log.ts\",\"sandbox.d.ts\",\"scratch.ts\",\"summary.ts\",\"tool-contract.ts\",\"workspace.ts\"],\"returned\":21,\"observed\":21,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":459,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\