ssfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Dans explore.ts, comment la branche memory_run retrouve-t-elle la fonction enregistrée ? Lis uniquement les lignes 334 à 348 et réponds avec citations. Signale que son exécution est hors périmètre."}],"options":{"maxOutputTokens":16384,"codeMode":true,"memory":true}}
