{"level":30,"time":1794927137639,"pid":93797,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"f3e8dfee-7ee1-4075-b616-68bf2405b280","event":"model_response","response":{"result":{"candidate":{"name":"traceCallContext","question":"How does cli.ts launch explore after the sandbox preflight?","description":"Locates every occurrence of a symbol (e.g. 'explore') in a target file using a repository-wide exact-identifier and literal-text search, then reads a bounded window of lines around each hit to expose the surrounding control flow (guards, preflight blocks, await calls, emit). Output is an object { file, symbol, contexts } where each context contains the anchor hit {file, line, text} plus the raw lines of the window. Scope: syntactic evidence only, no semantic resolution or proof of absence. Limits: occurrences capped by limit (default 5), window size capped by context lines on each side (default 12), search hits capped at 50 before filtering by file.","source":"async function traceCallContext(\n  params: { file: string; symbol: string; context?: number; limit?: number },\n  primitives: {\n    findSymbolOccurrences: (args: { symbol: string; limit?: number }) => Promise<{ file: string; line: number; text: string }[]>;\n    readLines: (args: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number }) => Promise<unknown>;\n  }\n) {\n  const { file, symbol, context = 12, limit = 5 } = params;\n  const hits = await primitives.findSymbolOccurrences({ symbol, limit: 50 });\n  const inFile = hits.filter(h => h.file === file).slice(0, limit);\n  const contexts: Array<{ anchor: { file: string; line: number; text: string }; startLine: number; endLine: number; lines: unknown[] }> = [];\n  for (const hit of inFile) {\n    const startLine = Math.max(1, hit.line - context);\n    const endLine = hit.line + context;\n    const raw = await primitives.readLines({ file, startLine, endLine });\n    const lines: unknown[] = Array.isArray(raw)\n      ? raw\n      : raw && typeof raw === 'object' && 'result' in raw && raw.result && typeof raw.result === 'object' && Array.isArray((raw.result as any).lines)\n        ? (raw.result as any).lines\n        : [];\n    contexts.push({ anchor: { file: hit.file, line: hit.line, text: hit.text }, startLine, endLine, lines });\n  }\n  return { file, symbol, contexts };\n}","params":{"file":"string — target file to filter hits and read windows from (e.g. 'cli.ts')","symbol":"string — exact identifier to locate (e.g. 'explore')","context":"number | undefined — lines read before and after each hit (default 12)","limit":"number | undefined — maximum contexts returned (default 5)"}}},"usage":{"inputTokens":1967,"outputTokens":1787}},"model":{"model":"zai-glm-5-3-flash","temperature":0,"maxOutputTokens":16384}}
