 (ligne 97) sont appelés dans la fenêtre mais définis ailleurs : non examinés.\",\"Le préflight n'est exécuté que si codeMode est vrai (garde ligne 98) ; explore est appelée inconditionnellement (ligne 111) une fois le flux atteint, mais l'existence d'éventuels early returns entre les lignes 90-97 et après 112 n'est pas vérifiable dans la fenêtre imposée.\",\"Recherche purement syntaxique sur la fenêtre fournie ; aucune résolution sémantique des identifiants n'a été effectuée.\"]},\"catalog\":[{\"id\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"objective\":\"How does loadConfig load configuration in config.ts?\",\"description\":\"Searches a repository for occurrences of a symbol by exact identifier match and literal text match, deduplicates by file:line, and returns up to limit {file, line, text} candidates. Scope: syntactic search only, no semantic resolution. Limits: capped by limit (default 3); text may be empty.\",\"parameters\":[\"limit\",\"symbol\"],\"paramsSchema\":[{\"name\":\"symbol\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"limit\",\"type\":\"number | undefined\"}],\"outputContract\":{\"returns\":\"{ file: string; line: number; text: string; }[]\",\"itemFields\":[\"file\",\"line\"],\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000}},\"limits\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"uncertaintyCases\":[],\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\"}],\"calls\":[{\"name\":\"readLines\",\"parameters\":{\"endLine\":112,\"file\":\"cli.ts\",\"startLine\":90},\"result\":{\"result\":{\"file\":\"cli.ts\",\"start\":90,\"lines\":[{\"line\":90,\"text\":\"const canonicalMemory = join(root, '.tours', '.memory');\"},{\"line\":91,\"text\":\"if (legacyMemory && resolve(legacyMemory) !== canonicalMemory) throw new Error(`Memory must be stored at ${canonicalMemory}`);\"},{\"line\":92,\"text\":\"const memory = memoryEnabled ? { directory: canonicalMemory } : undefined;\"},{\"line\":93,\"text\":\"// .tours/config.json holds every setting; CLI options override it per run. Only the API key may also come from the environment.\"},{\"line\":94,\"text\":\"const config = await loadConfig(root);\"},{\"line\":95,\"text\":\"const effectiveTemperature = temperature ?? config.mistral.temperature;\"},{\"line\":96,\"text\":\"if (!Number.isFinite(effectiveTemperature) || effectiveTemperature < 0 || effectiveTemperature > 1) throw new Error('Temperature must be between 0 and 1');\"},{\"line\":97,\"text\":\"model = mistral(process.env.MISTRAL_API_KEY || config.mistral.apiKey, modelName ?? config.mistral.model, { ...config.mistral, temperature: effectiveTemperature });\"},{\"line\":98,\"text\":\"if (codeMode) {\"},{\"line\":99,\"text\":\"  // Exercise the real sandbox before starting a model run, including QuickJS and TypeScript.\"},{\"line\":100,\"text\":\"  const { runScript } = await import('codetour-exploration-sandbox');\"},{\"line\":101,\"text\":\"  try { await runScript({ workspace: root, code: '() => 1', params: {}, strict: true, timeoutMs: config.limits.scriptTimeoutMs }); }\"},{\"line\":102,\"text\":\"  catch (error) { throw new Error(`Sandbox preflight failed: ${(error as Error).message}`); }\"},{\"line\":103,\"text\":\"}\"},{\"line\":104,\"text\":\"// Progress is appended as JSON lines next to the output file so a long run can be followed with tail -f.\"},{\"line\":105,\"text\":\"let onProgress: ((event: Record<string, unknown>) => void) | undefined;\"},{\"line\":106,\"text\":\"if (outputFile) {\"},{\"line\":107,\"text\":\"  const progressFile = `${outputFile}.progress`;\"},{\"line\":108,\"text\":\"  await writeFile(progressFile, '');\"},{\"line\":109,\"text\":\"  onProgress = event => appendFileSync(progressFile, `${JSON.stringify(event)}\\\\n`);\"},{\"line\":110,\"text\":\"}\"},{\"line\":111,\"text\":\"const result = await explore({ root, objective, codeMode, memory, budget, model, config, onProgress });\"},{\"line\":112,\"text\":\"await emit(result);\"}],\"nextLine\":null,\"truncatedLines\":[]},\"returned\":1,\"observed\":null,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":2291,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"]}}],\"previousAttempts\":[{\"candidate\":{\"name\":\"traceCallContext\",\"question\":\"How does cli.ts launch explore after the sandbox preflight?\",\"description\":\"Locates every occurrence of a symbol (e.g. 'explore') in a target file using a repository-wide exact-identifier and literal-text search, then reads a bounded window of lines around each hit to expose the surrounding control flow (guards, preflight blocks, await calls, emit). Output is an object { file, symbol, contexts } where each context contains the anchor hit {file, line, text} plus the raw lines of the window. Scope: syntactic evidence only, no semantic resolution or proof of absence. Limits: occurrences capped by limit (default 5), window size capped by context lines on each side (default 12), search hits capped at 50 before filtering by file.\",\"source\":\"async function traceCallContext(\\n  params: { file: string; symbol: string; context?: number; limit?: number },\\n  primitives: {\\n    findSymbolOccurrences: (args: { symbol: string; limit?: number }) => Promise<{ file: string; line: number; text: string }[]>;\\n    readLines: (args: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number }) => Promise<unknown>;\\n  }\\n) {\\n  const { file, symbol, context = 12, limit = 5 } = params;\\n  const hits = await primitives.findSymbolOccurrences({ symbol, limit: 50 });\\n  const inFile = hits.filter(h => h.file === file).slice(0, limit);\\n  const contexts: Array<{ anchor: { file: string; line: number; text: string }; startLine: number; endLine: number; lines: unknown[] }> = [];\\n  for (const hit of inFile) {\\n    const startLine = Math.max(1, hit.line - context);\\n    const endLine = hit.line + context;\\n    const raw = await primitives.readLines({ file, startLine, endLine });\\n    const lines: unknown[] = Array.isArray(raw)\\n      ? raw\\n      : raw && typeof raw === 'object' && 'result' in raw && raw.result && typeof raw.result === 'object' && Array.isArray((raw.result as any).lines)\\n        ? (raw.result as any).lines\\n        : [];\\n    contexts.push({ anchor: { file: hit.file, line: hit.line, text: hit.text }, startLine, endLine, lines });\\n  }\\n  return { file, symbol, contexts };\\n}\",\"params\":{\"file\":\"string — target file to filter hits and read windows from (e.g. 'cli.ts')\",\"symbol\":\"string — exact identifier to locate (e.g. 'explore')\",\"context\":\"number | undefined — lines read before and after each hit (default 12)\",\"limit\":\"number | undefined — maximum contexts returned (default 5)\"}},\"error\":\"Description is too long: 657 characters; at most 300 are allowed.\"}]}"}],"options":{"maxOutputTokens":16384,"codeMode":false,"memory":false,"toolsEnabled":false}}
{"level":30,"time":1794927142216,"pid":93797,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"f3e8dfee-7ee1-4075-b616-68bf2405b280","event":"model_response","response":{"result":{"candidate":{"name":"traceSymbolWindows","question":"How does cli.ts launch explore after the sandbox preflight?","description":"Finds occurrences of a symbol in a file via exact-identifier search, then reads a bounded line window around each hit to expose surrounding control flow. Returns {file, symbol, contexts} with anchor hit and raw lines. Syntactic evidence only; no semantic resolution. Caps: limit hits, context lines per side.","source":"async function traceSymbolWindows(\n  params: { file: string; symbol: string; context?: number; limit?: number },\n  primitives: {\n    findSymbolOccurrences: (args: { symbol: string; limit?: number }) => Promise<{ file: string; line: number; text: string }[]>;\n    readLines: (args: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number }) => Promise<unknown>;\n  }\n) {\n  const { file, symbol, context = 12, limit = 5 } = params;\n  const hits = await primitives.findSymbolOccurrences({ symbol, limit: 50 });\n  const inFile = hits.filter(h => h.file === file).slice(0, limit);\n  const contexts: Array<{ anchor: { file: string; line: number; text: string }; startLine: number; endLine: number; lines: unknown[] }> = [];\n  for (const hit of inFile) {\n    const startLine = Math.max(1, hit.line - context);\n    const endLine = hit.line + context;\n    const raw = await primitives.readLines({ file, startLine, endLine });\n    const lines: unknown[] = Array.isArray(raw)\n      ? raw\n      : raw && typeof raw === 'object' && 'result' in raw && raw.result && typeof raw.result === 'object' && Array.isArray((raw.result as any).lines)\n        ? (raw.result as any).lines\n        : [];\n    contexts.push({ anchor: { file: hit.file, line: hit.line, text: hit.text }, startLine, endLine, lines });\n  }\n  return { file, symbol, contexts };\n}","params":{"file":"string — target file to filter hits and read windows from (e.g. 'cli.ts')","symbol":"string — exact identifier to locate (e.g. 'explore')","context":"number | undefined — lines read before and after each hit (default 12)","limit":"number | undefined — maximum contexts returned (default 5)"}}},"usage":{"inputTokens":2610,"outputTokens":810}},"model":{"model":"zai-glm-5-3-flash","temperature":0,"maxOutputTokens":16384}}
